WEBVTT

00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:44.250
I'm...

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:45.750
back...

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:48.350
Hi!

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:49.220
Hi.

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:53.520
Where's the manager?

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:54.960
She went to her
parents' place.

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:58.330
Her mother's really ill
with a cold or something.

00:01:58.710 --> 00:01:59.580
Really?

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:01.740
What's with that look?

00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:04.040
Maybe they're making her meet
another prospective husband.

00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:06.840
Well, that is a possibility.

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:09.480
It's not often she gets to
help her parents out.

00:02:09.650 --> 00:02:12.150
It's not like
she's never coming back.

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:14.210
T-That's right.

00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:19.150
She is coming back,
isn't she?

00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:38.300
Daddy, carry me!

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:42.180
No, Etchan.
Your Dad's exhausted.

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:45.650
I'm all right. Just a minute...

00:02:48.170 --> 00:02:48.680
There!

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:52.680
Yay!

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:01.700
I'm home.

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:05.170
Ritsuko, how are you feeling?

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:06.870
Hi, Dad!

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:08.980
K-Kyoko?!

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:12.310
W-What're you doing here?

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:15.340
Kyoko, why are you...?

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:16.680
Kyoko!

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:21.310
Can't you tell?
I'm here to fill in for Mom!

00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:24.710
I see. You came here for us.

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:26.050
I see.

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:26.990
Dad, your shoes.

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:27.710
Oops.

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:31.990
I'm carrying my shoe...

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:36.960
Hey! Mom! Kyoko's here.

00:03:37.370 --> 00:03:40.830
Why are you yelling
like a child?

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:43.640
It's Kyoko! Kyoko's here!

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:46.010
I asked her to come.

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:48.810
Why did you bring
your shoe in here?

00:03:48.890 --> 00:03:51.400
What? Oh, this...

00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:56.580
He sounds so happy.

00:04:05.830 --> 00:04:09.930
Delicious. I'm so glad
I asked you to come.

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:20.540
I haven't been able to
take care of your dad lately.

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:23.310
Whenever she pushed herself,
her fever came back.

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:26.780
Must have been hard.
Here, Dad.

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:28.690
Ohh. Thanks.

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:36.320
We're so glad you're here.

00:04:42.310 --> 00:04:47.140
Oh? So she'll be gone
for 2-3 days?

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:50.200
It's lonely without her.

00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:53.380
It's like the lights have gone out.

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:54.580
Yeah, right!!

00:04:57.080 --> 00:04:59.710
Weren't you studying?

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:03.420
Even with my headphones on, when
you're making such a racket...

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:05.330
I can hear you!

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:07.590
Let's see...

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:12.060
It's an English lesson!

00:05:13.530 --> 00:05:15.080
How could you!

00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:19.330
I know you're sad...

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:23.170
but I'll take good care
of you while the manager's away.

00:05:23.390 --> 00:05:26.040
Oh, you're so nice!

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:28.640
You're like
a manager yourself.

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:31.150
Don't be ridiculous!

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:36.460
The bathroom light bulb
is still out...

00:05:36.590 --> 00:05:39.020
and no one's fixed
the leaking faucet.

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:45.480
Godai, does the manager's job
include fixing these, too?

00:05:45.710 --> 00:05:47.140
It broke open...

00:05:47.770 --> 00:05:50.070
That cost me 38,000 yen.

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:54.350
-What'll we do?
-Dunno.

00:05:54.450 --> 00:05:56.460
No way we can fix that!

00:06:05.020 --> 00:06:08.460
Two, three days went right by.

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:16.200
Mom, you seem to be
doing really well now.

00:06:16.570 --> 00:06:17.780
You think so?

00:06:19.140 --> 00:06:20.460
I wonder.

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:23.730
I still feel weak.

00:06:24.340 --> 00:06:25.400
Let's see.

00:06:26.340 --> 00:06:30.510
I think you're still feverish.
Say "ah."

00:06:32.150 --> 00:06:34.120
I think your tonsils
are still swollen.

00:06:34.190 --> 00:06:34.710
Oh?

00:06:35.480 --> 00:06:39.950
One, two. One, two. One, two.

00:06:56.950 --> 00:07:00.010
I WILL BE BACK IN 2-3 DAYS
--MANAGER

00:07:08.830 --> 00:07:11.450
Four days went by,
and five days went by...

00:07:11.960 --> 00:07:14.040
but the manager
didn't come back.

00:07:23.160 --> 00:07:26.500
I wonder when
she's coming back?

00:07:38.390 --> 00:07:40.340
Hey, Soichiro!
Let's go for a walk.

00:08:08.270 --> 00:08:09.290
Uh...

00:08:09.390 --> 00:08:11.780
Mr. Ichinose!
You're home already?

00:08:11.850 --> 00:08:14.380
Uh-huh. I had the early shift.

00:08:15.320 --> 00:08:18.270
You weren't waiting
for the manager?

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:21.020
N-No. I was just
walking the dog.

00:08:24.090 --> 00:08:26.710
How about a drink?

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:27.770
Oh, uh...

00:08:31.610 --> 00:08:34.730
Sorry I dragged you along.

00:08:34.850 --> 00:08:36.200
Not at all.

00:08:37.670 --> 00:08:41.630
You think the manager's mother
is really that ill?

00:08:42.220 --> 00:08:43.110
I don't know.

00:08:48.390 --> 00:08:49.850
Is something the matter?

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:58.730
Watching you brings back
the days of my youth.

00:09:00.370 --> 00:09:02.360
I had one, too...

00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:05.550
a woman I adored.

00:09:15.540 --> 00:09:17.700
I guess she's what you call...

00:09:19.050 --> 00:09:21.070
a "jewel in a dunghill."

00:09:23.420 --> 00:09:30.260
She was at a tiny little company
where I was hired after college.

00:09:38.980 --> 00:09:40.000
Thanks.

00:09:48.810 --> 00:09:51.650
She made me happy
just looking at her.

00:09:52.590 --> 00:09:56.310
I made excuses just to be
able to talk to her.

00:09:58.130 --> 00:10:00.780
Why do I remind you
of all that?

00:10:02.130 --> 00:10:05.280
One night,
we had a company party.

00:10:13.400 --> 00:10:18.420
I was hoping that this would give
me a chance to get to know her.

00:10:19.520 --> 00:10:20.850
But it was that night--

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:24.140
Mr. Ichinose, wanna have
a drinking contest?

00:10:24.360 --> 00:10:25.750
Yeah! Great idea!

00:10:26.310 --> 00:10:28.220
I heard you can
really drink, too.

00:10:29.230 --> 00:10:32.810
Hanae was one year
senior to that woman.

00:10:32.950 --> 00:10:33.810
"Hanae"?

00:10:34.520 --> 00:10:35.990
Her name is beautiful
isn't it?

00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:41.820
Hanae, if this is a contest
there's gotta be a prize.

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:43.820
That's true.

00:10:44.900 --> 00:10:47.840
If you win, Mr. Ichinose,
I'll be your wife.

00:10:49.400 --> 00:10:50.240
Yay!

00:10:50.570 --> 00:10:54.240
We'll be the judge.
Drink till one of you drops!

00:10:54.770 --> 00:10:56.270
I'll take care of the bill!

00:10:57.750 --> 00:11:00.610
I told myself, "Do not win."

00:11:01.320 --> 00:11:03.590
Th-Then how did you win?

00:11:06.190 --> 00:11:08.250
She told me after
we got married...

00:11:08.320 --> 00:11:12.260
but Hanae had pretended
to be drunk.

00:11:13.470 --> 00:11:16.420
Oh, Boy. I just can't--

00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:20.160
I lose! I'll marry you
like I promised!

00:11:20.380 --> 00:11:21.800
No! I--

00:11:22.480 --> 00:11:23.800
That's entrapment!

00:11:25.380 --> 00:11:28.530
Apparently, it was just her
own way of proposing to me.

00:11:29.650 --> 00:11:31.430
Another sake, please.

00:11:33.180 --> 00:11:34.020
Here you go.

00:11:34.310 --> 00:11:37.840
And I just went along with it.

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:41.480
But you know...

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:52.230
Now, I'm happy
that I married her.

00:12:00.170 --> 00:12:02.430
Is that...how it goes?

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:04.510
Uh-huh.

00:12:06.890 --> 00:12:08.270
Shall we get going?

00:12:08.490 --> 00:12:10.110
Thanks!

00:12:15.600 --> 00:12:16.360
Um...

00:12:18.020 --> 00:12:20.650
That "jewel in
a dunghill" woman...

00:12:21.370 --> 00:12:22.790
Where is she now?

00:12:23.510 --> 00:12:28.520
I don't know. I'm sure
she's happy somewhere.

00:12:32.250 --> 00:12:34.930
Jewel in a dunghill...

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:58.620
I haven't eaten in
the kitchen in a while!

00:13:00.610 --> 00:13:02.500
Mom, you're all right now,
aren't you?

00:13:03.080 --> 00:13:06.030
I'd like to go
back to Maison Ik--

00:13:06.120 --> 00:13:09.910
That reminds me! Remember
when Kyoko was in high school?

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:12.890
Oh, yeah. She was
in high school!

00:13:12.990 --> 00:13:13.670
Right?

00:13:13.750 --> 00:13:17.270
Yeah. She used to eat
a lot of peanuts.

00:13:18.420 --> 00:13:21.830
I can't let that building go
for more than a week.

00:13:25.940 --> 00:13:29.020
This is a very critical stage
in getting over a cold.

00:13:30.400 --> 00:13:32.240
You're fine.

00:13:32.870 --> 00:13:36.500
What do you mean?! She needs to
rest for two, three more days.

00:13:40.090 --> 00:13:43.610
Let's see... I ate the toast
drank my milk--

00:13:43.750 --> 00:13:45.270
Dad, it's time.

00:13:45.620 --> 00:13:48.800
That's right!
Gotta go to work!

00:13:49.620 --> 00:13:51.620
I'm going to come home
early today.

00:13:52.790 --> 00:13:53.650
See you.

00:13:53.870 --> 00:13:55.410
Have a nice day.

00:13:56.420 --> 00:13:58.190
Make sure you
don't let her go.

00:13:58.440 --> 00:14:01.790
We are going to enjoy our time
as a family as long as possible.

00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:05.200
Who knows when she'll be
back again if she leaves.

00:14:05.270 --> 00:14:06.130
Keep her here.

00:14:08.480 --> 00:14:09.660
What were you talking about?

00:14:09.750 --> 00:14:10.970
Oh...

00:14:11.540 --> 00:14:12.370
nothing.

00:14:13.120 --> 00:14:16.450
I really need to go
back to Maison Ikkoku.

00:14:18.490 --> 00:14:19.770
I'm the manager.

00:14:20.010 --> 00:14:21.740
I have responsibilities there.

00:14:21.830 --> 00:14:24.510
They'll call you
if they need you...

00:14:25.600 --> 00:14:27.220
and no one's called yet.

00:14:27.390 --> 00:14:28.590
It's fine.

00:14:29.160 --> 00:14:31.390
But I thought I'd be here
just two or three days...

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:33.790
so I didn't bring
much change of clothes.

00:14:37.110 --> 00:14:39.570
Go shopping.
I'll give you money.

00:14:39.670 --> 00:14:41.660
Don't be silly.
That's being wasteful.

00:14:45.410 --> 00:14:48.820
You know, you ought to think
about your father.

00:14:55.860 --> 00:14:57.750
Your father and I are not
trying to keep you here...

00:14:57.830 --> 00:14:59.780
because we want you
to quit your job...

00:14:59.860 --> 00:15:02.870
or change your name back,
or get remarried...

00:15:02.970 --> 00:15:05.370
or anything like that.

00:15:08.610 --> 00:15:10.840
Have we said any of this?

00:15:11.270 --> 00:15:14.760
All we want to do is enjoy
having you around.

00:15:14.980 --> 00:15:16.130
Well...

00:15:17.040 --> 00:15:19.740
You had me around
for more than a week!

00:15:19.880 --> 00:15:20.500
Right?

00:15:20.750 --> 00:15:22.530
You really want
to go so badly?!

00:15:22.620 --> 00:15:24.160
Let me go without
making me feel bad!

00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:30.090
Because...because I...

00:15:30.150 --> 00:15:31.010
What?

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:34.280
I can't get a good night's
rest without my own pillow.

00:15:35.100 --> 00:15:36.380
Pillow?

00:15:37.070 --> 00:15:40.890
Uh-huh. It's got to be the
one I use at Maison Ikkoku.

00:15:42.240 --> 00:15:46.750
Really? Pillow?
I see! A pillow!

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:52.980
Time out!

00:15:53.820 --> 00:15:55.140
Yes, yes, yes...

00:15:55.540 --> 00:15:57.450
This is Maison Ikkoku.

00:15:58.990 --> 00:16:00.370
The manager's mother!?

00:16:00.860 --> 00:16:02.820
What? Her pillow?

00:16:03.150 --> 00:16:05.910
Yes, she insists!

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:07.010
Mom!

00:16:07.920 --> 00:16:08.860
Hello?

00:16:10.200 --> 00:16:10.780
Godai?

00:16:11.100 --> 00:16:12.520
M-Manager!

00:16:15.760 --> 00:16:19.720
It's no trouble! I have time.
I'll take it to you right away!

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:22.200
What? N-No, wait--

00:16:23.710 --> 00:16:25.290
Where're you going?

00:16:25.620 --> 00:16:28.400
Back off! I have
an important errand to run!

00:16:30.510 --> 00:16:31.850
What'll I do...?

00:16:34.780 --> 00:16:35.540
Here.

00:16:36.620 --> 00:16:38.640
You sure she wants you
to bring this?

00:16:38.730 --> 00:16:41.910
That's what
the manager's mother said.

00:16:48.530 --> 00:16:50.650
I'll take this to her.

00:16:51.210 --> 00:16:51.750
No!

00:16:52.030 --> 00:16:53.050
If you take it...

00:16:53.130 --> 00:16:55.970
you'll sniff at it and nuzzle it
and make it smelly.

00:16:56.110 --> 00:16:57.070
Eww!

00:16:57.950 --> 00:17:00.440
Give it back!
I'll give you instant noodles!

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:04.210
I want a cutlet bowl!

00:17:05.890 --> 00:17:07.980
All right!!

00:17:11.700 --> 00:17:12.850
That's a promise!

00:17:14.160 --> 00:17:17.080
This is my ticket to see Kyoko!

00:17:28.210 --> 00:17:29.290
I'm off!

00:17:32.010 --> 00:17:33.800
What's he thinking?

00:17:33.880 --> 00:17:35.740
Maybe he thinks he's going
to talk marriage.

00:17:36.890 --> 00:17:44.990
Donning a suit
A young stallion woos
The woman of his dreams

00:17:50.360 --> 00:17:53.200
CHIGUSA

00:18:15.550 --> 00:18:16.180
Hey, you--

00:18:21.790 --> 00:18:24.080
You are--

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:29.900
I'm Godai.

00:18:29.970 --> 00:18:31.490
That's right.

00:18:31.570 --> 00:18:33.590
You're the college student.

00:18:35.540 --> 00:18:36.640
Dad!

00:18:37.540 --> 00:18:39.030
I'm home.

00:18:40.110 --> 00:18:41.270
Hello.

00:18:43.610 --> 00:18:45.000
Godai...

00:18:45.550 --> 00:18:48.510
So you brought Kyoko's pillow
all the way here?

00:18:48.580 --> 00:18:50.490
Thank you so much
for your trouble.

00:18:50.660 --> 00:18:52.510
Not at all.

00:18:53.200 --> 00:18:56.430
Enough formalities.
Make yourself at home.

00:19:02.140 --> 00:19:04.320
I'm sorry, Godai.

00:19:04.530 --> 00:19:05.430
No problem.

00:19:13.920 --> 00:19:15.710
But what is he doing...

00:19:16.810 --> 00:19:18.360
wearing a suit?

00:19:18.510 --> 00:19:20.950
So, you...
What year are you now?

00:19:22.520 --> 00:19:24.990
My name is Godai.
I'll be a senior.

00:19:25.350 --> 00:19:28.250
Then you'll be
job-hunting soon?

00:19:28.320 --> 00:19:28.840
Yes.

00:19:30.170 --> 00:19:31.820
Where are you
planning to apply?

00:19:31.970 --> 00:19:34.630
Well...I'm not sure yet.

00:19:34.860 --> 00:19:35.490
What?

00:19:39.100 --> 00:19:42.090
Oops. I'd better
sound more confident.

00:19:43.100 --> 00:19:47.290
Well, I'd like to apply
to the big corporations.

00:19:49.340 --> 00:19:50.680
What college do you attend?

00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:54.810
Don't be rude with
so many questions.

00:19:55.020 --> 00:19:56.780
Godai, I'm sorry.

00:19:57.080 --> 00:19:57.880
It's okay.

00:19:58.820 --> 00:20:02.630
It's not such an
embarrassing school, really.

00:20:03.200 --> 00:20:05.690
Well, thank you for
what you've done today.

00:20:05.900 --> 00:20:08.460
Now Kyoko can stay longer.

00:20:08.830 --> 00:20:09.430
What?

00:20:10.100 --> 00:20:11.320
Really?

00:20:12.880 --> 00:20:14.800
I never said that!

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:16.940
I said I need to go back
to sleep on my own pillow.

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:20.130
So, Mr. Student, you must have
a girlfriend, don't you?

00:20:33.700 --> 00:20:35.390
I don't have a girlfriend...

00:20:36.090 --> 00:20:39.390
but I am in love with someone.

00:20:40.740 --> 00:20:42.590
Unrequited love?

00:20:43.030 --> 00:20:44.520
Yes, well...

00:20:44.600 --> 00:20:45.700
What's she like?

00:20:46.140 --> 00:20:48.000
Mom! Stop it!

00:20:49.800 --> 00:20:50.460
Well...

00:20:52.040 --> 00:20:54.910
She has long hair...

00:20:55.540 --> 00:20:56.760
and she's kind.

00:20:58.610 --> 00:20:59.410
And...

00:21:00.750 --> 00:21:02.690
she's two years
older than me.

00:21:04.230 --> 00:21:06.220
And she's very adorable.

00:21:08.130 --> 00:21:09.340
It's hard to explain.

00:21:10.360 --> 00:21:11.790
Two years older?

00:21:12.030 --> 00:21:14.080
Is she a working woman?

00:21:14.330 --> 00:21:14.890
Yes.

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:18.470
Cut it out, Mom.
It's none of our business.

00:21:18.830 --> 00:21:21.020
Why not?!

00:21:21.480 --> 00:21:23.200
He's enjoying his youth.

00:21:23.600 --> 00:21:26.170
So what does she do?

00:21:26.610 --> 00:21:27.640
Mom!

00:21:28.220 --> 00:21:29.710
S-She's...

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:32.750
She's a manag--

00:21:45.640 --> 00:21:47.320
She's a m-managerial officer.

00:21:48.100 --> 00:21:49.660
Managerial officer?

00:21:50.940 --> 00:21:51.580
Yes.

00:21:55.650 --> 00:21:56.630
Godai.

00:21:56.710 --> 00:21:57.230
Yes!

00:21:57.610 --> 00:22:03.450
So, it sounds like this woman
you're in love with...

00:22:13.160 --> 00:22:14.250
I...

00:22:15.260 --> 00:22:17.520
The woman you're in
love with must be...

00:22:18.530 --> 00:22:20.760
a very admirable woman.

00:22:26.380 --> 00:22:29.210
But if she's so admirable...

00:22:29.270 --> 00:22:31.360
you really have to become
worthy of her.

00:22:32.480 --> 00:22:35.210
You're so right about that.

00:22:53.260 --> 00:22:56.200
I wonder if Kyoko
got what I said?

00:22:57.500 --> 00:22:58.860
She must have.

00:23:05.040 --> 00:23:07.030
What's Kyoko doing?

00:23:10.420 --> 00:23:12.980
She must really love
that pillow of hers.

00:23:14.610 --> 00:23:15.770
Whatever.

00:23:16.020 --> 00:23:18.720
Whatever it takes to
make her stay a bit longer.

00:23:19.230 --> 00:23:21.490
You gave me quite
a big shock, Godai.

00:23:22.520 --> 00:23:26.250
Those words were so unexpected.

00:23:27.090 --> 00:23:28.110
I--

00:23:36.770 --> 00:23:37.500
But...

00:23:39.480 --> 00:23:40.590
thank you.

00:23:50.300 --> 00:23:53.930
I had a hunch
but Mitaka really hates dogs.

00:23:54.010 --> 00:23:55.880
Yeah? I thought so.

00:23:56.120 --> 00:23:59.680
Next: "Mitaka's 'Call of the Wild'!
How Can You Love When You Fear?"

00:23:59.890 --> 00:24:02.080
Dogs know who's boss.

00:24:02.750 --> 00:24:06.160
Let us train you!
